@node Interfaces
@chapter Interfaces
@cindex interface control document
@cindex ICD

This chapter is the interface control document (Standard §23.2;
ESC-SRS-089).  It was drafted at gate G2 and is completed in M5; it is
frozen at G3.  Every interface has its own version, which changes only when
the interface does.  Data interfaces carry a committed JSON Schema under
@file{schemas/}, which the tests validate against.  An interface with no
declared class would be stable by default; every one here declares one.

@menu
* Interface inventory::   Every interface, its version and class.
* CLI interface::         Commands, global flags, output, errors, exit codes.
* Configuration format::  The TOML file and the mapping grammar.
* Environment interface:: Variables Escape Pod reads.
* Status socket::         The daemon's JSON Lines protocol.
* Packaging surface::     Paths, units, rules and accounts.
@end menu

@node Interface inventory
@section Interface inventory

@table @asis
@item CLI command tree and flags
Class: Command-line surface.  Version 1, unstable.  Schema and consumers: @code{escapepod schema}; users, agents, the systemd unit.
@item JSON envelope and errors
Class: Machine-readable output.  Version 1, unstable.  Schema and consumers: @file{schemas/envelope.schema.json}; agents, @code{daemon status}.
@item Exit codes 0 to 6
Class: Command-line surface.  Version 1, stable.  Schema and consumers: none (a table); the systemd unit (@code{RestartPreventExitStatus=6}).
@item Configuration file
Class: On-disk and configuration.  Version 1, unstable.  Schema and consumers: @file{schemas/config.schema.json}; users, the NixOS module.
@item xcape mapping grammar
Class: Command-line surface.  Version 1, stable.  Schema and consumers: none (a grammar); former xcape users.
@item Status socket protocol
Class: Wire and IPC.  Version 1, unstable.  Schema and consumers: @file{schemas/status.schema.json}; @code{daemon status}.
@item Environment variables
Class: Environment variables.  Version 1, stable.  Schema and consumers: none; agent harnesses, terminals.
@item Paths and packaging surface
Class: Filesystem layout.  Version 1, unstable.  Schema and consumers: none; packagers, the NixOS module.
@item Crate APIs
Class: Library API.  Version 0, internal.  Schema and consumers: none; the workspace's own crates only (unpublished).
@end table

Each interface's contract (names, types, ranges, units, encodings, error
behaviour) is written as its own node when the interface is built: the CLI
and JSON output in M2, the socket in M3, the packaging surface in M5.

@node CLI interface
@section CLI interface (version 1, unstable)

@table @asis
@item Commands
@code{daemon run}, @code{daemon status}, @code{event monitor},
@code{device list}, @code{config check}, @code{schema [@var{noun}
[@var{verb}]]}, @code{describe}.  @code{run} is a human alias of
@code{daemon run} and never appears in @code{schema} or @code{describe}.
@item Global flags
@option{--json}, @option{--format json|jsonl|yaml|csv|explore},
@option{--fields @var{f1,f2}}, @option{--dry-run}, @option{-v}/@option{--verbose},
@option{-q}/@option{--quiet}, @option{--no-color},
@option{--color never|always|auto}, @option{--version},
@option{--absolute-time}, @option{-0}/@option{--print0},
@option{--yes}/@option{--force}, @option{--accessible},
@option{--config @var{path}}.  @option{--quiet} with @option{--verbose}
is a usage error.  @option{explore} is accepted and falls back to JSON with
a @code{TUI_FALLBACK} warning: Escape Pod has no TUI.
@item Mapping flags
@option{--map @var{KEY=TAP[;KEY=TAP]...}} and @option{--tap-timeout @var{ms}}
(50 to 2000) on @code{daemon run}, @code{config check} and
@code{event monitor}; @option{--backend auto|evdev|x11} on @code{daemon run}.
@item Output selection
An explicit format wins; else an agent environment selects JSON; else a
terminal selects human text; else JSON.  Human text is UTF-8 and parses with
@command{awk}; JSON is compact, one document, on standard output only.
@item Envelope
One object with @code{metadata} (@code{tool}, @code{version},
@code{command}, @code{timestamp}) and @code{data}, committed as
@file{schemas/envelope.schema.json}.  Timestamps are ISO 8601
UTC with @samp{Z}, whole seconds.
@item Errors
One compact line on standard error: an object with one key, @code{error},
holding @code{code}, @code{exit_code}, @code{message}, @code{hint},
@code{timestamp}, @code{command} and @code{docs_url}, with extended fields @code{path}, @code{line},
@code{column} or @code{position} where they apply.  The hint is a command
runnable without privileges, or @samp{human:} and an action.  Human mode
prints @samp{[ERROR] @var{message}} and an indented @samp{hint:} line.
@item Diagnostics
An object with one key, @code{diagnostic}, holding @code{severity},
@code{code}, @code{message}, @code{hint}, @code{timestamp} and
@code{command}, for @samp{warn}, @samp{ok} and @samp{info};
human mode prints @samp{[WARN]}, @samp{[OK]}, @samp{[INFO]}.  The floor is
@samp{error} under @option{--quiet}, @samp{info} under @option{--verbose},
@samp{warn} under @env{AI_AGENT} or @env{AGENT}, else @samp{ok}.
@item Exit codes (stable)
0 success; 1 general failure; 2 usage or configuration error; 3 not found;
4 permission denied or no backend; 5 conflict; 6 emergency release, produced
only by the emergency chord.
@end table

@node Configuration format
@section Configuration format (version 1, unstable)

TOML, UTF-8, read from @option{--config}, else
@file{$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/escapepod/config.toml} (or
@file{~/.config/escapepod/config.toml}), else
@file{/etc/escapepod/config.toml}.  Every table rejects unknown keys
(exit 2, with the line and column).

@table @code
@item grab
@samp{all} (default): every keyboard is grabbed unless a rule ignores it;
@samp{listed}: only keyboards a @code{[[device]]} rule names.
@item tap_timeout_ms
Integer, 50 to 2000; default 200.
@item emergency_chord
Array of key names, at least one; default Backspace, Escape, Enter.
@item protected
Array of key names never mapped.
@item [[dual_role]]
@code{key} (physical key), @code{hold} (optional, defaults to @code{key}),
@code{tap}.
@item [[remap]]
@code{from}, @code{to}.
@item [[device]]
Exactly one of @code{name} (the kernel device name) or @code{id}
(@samp{VVVV:PPPP} in hexadecimal), and optionally @code{ignore},
@code{tap_timeout_ms}, @code{dual_role} and @code{remap}, which replace the
global lists for that device.  The first matching rule wins.
@end table

Key names are kernel names (@samp{KEY_CAPSLOCK}), kernel names without the
prefix (@samp{capslock}), or the X keysym names xcape uses
(@samp{Caps_Lock}, @samp{Control_L}, @samp{Escape}); case is ignored.
@option{--map} takes @samp{KEY=TAP} entries separated by @samp{;}; KEY is
both the physical and the hold key.  Multi-key taps (@samp{A|B}) are
refused.  @option{--map} replaces the global @code{dual_role} list, and
@option{--tap-timeout} every tap timeout.

@node Environment interface
@section Environment interface (version 1, stable)

@table @env
@item AI_AGENT
@itemx AGENT
Set to any non-empty value: agent environment (JSON, no colour, no prompts,
warning floor).
@item CI
Any value but @samp{0} or @samp{false}: agent environment.
@item NO_COLOR
@itemx FORCE_COLOR
@itemx CLICOLOR
@itemx TERM
Colour precedence, CLI Standard output-modes §6.
@item SPACECRAFT_THEME
A theme slug from the Steelbore palette contract; default @samp{steelbore}.
@item SPACECRAFT_A11Y
Any value but @samp{0} or @samp{false}: accessible mode.
@item XDG_CONFIG_HOME
@itemx XDG_DATA_HOME
@itemx HOME
The configuration search and the Orca settings file.
@item ESCAPEPOD_SYSFS
@itemx ESCAPEPOD_DEV_DIR
Replace @file{/sys/class/input} and @file{/dev/input}, for tests and
containers.
@item ESCAPEPOD_UINPUT
A node probed for read and write access before the virtual keyboard is
created on @file{/dev/uinput}; tests point it at a missing file to force
exit 4.
@item ESCAPEPOD_SOCKET
The status socket path, for the daemon and for @code{daemon status}.
@item XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The session daemon's socket directory.
@end table

@node Status socket
@section Status socket (version 1, unstable)

@table @asis
@item Path
For the service, @file{escapepod.sock} in @file{/run/escapepod}, a
directory of mode @samp{0750}, owner @samp{escapepod} and group
@samp{escapepod-ctl}.  For a session daemon, @file{escapepod.sock} in
@env{XDG_RUNTIME_DIR}.  @env{ESCAPEPOD_SOCKET} overrides both.
@item Access
Mode @samp{0660}, group @samp{escapepod-ctl}; @samp{0600} when that group
does not exist.
@item Framing
UTF-8 JSON Lines, one object per line, compact.
@item On connect
The daemon writes one status object: @code{backend}, @code{devices}
(@code{name}, @code{path}, @code{grabbed}), @code{pointers} (a count) and
@code{held} (the number of keys held, never which).  Schema:
@file{schemas/status.schema.json}.
@item Subscription
A client that writes @samp{events} receives one record per event of a
managed key: @code{timestamp}, @code{device}, @code{key}, @code{value}
(@samp{press}, @samp{release}, @samp{repeat}) and @code{decision}.  The key
code of an unmanaged key is never written.
@item Errors
A client that cannot be written to is dropped; a second daemon finding a live
socket exits 5.
@end table

@node Packaging surface
@section Packaging surface (version 1, unstable)

@table @asis
@item @file{bin/escapepod}
The binary.
@item @file{lib/systemd/system/escapepod.service}
Runs @code{daemon run --yes --backend evdev} with the configuration in @file{/etc/escapepod} as @samp{escapepod}; reload with @code{SIGHUP}; no restart after exit 6; @code{AF_UNIX} and @code{AF_NETLINK} only.
@item @file{lib/udev/rules.d/70-escapepod.rules}
Read ACL on event devices and group of @file{/dev/uinput}: @samp{escapepod} only.
@item @file{lib/sysusers.d/escapepod.conf}
Account @samp{escapepod}, groups @samp{escapepod} and @samp{escapepod-ctl}.
@item @file{lib/tmpfiles.d/escapepod.conf}
@file{/run/escapepod}.
@item @file{share/info/escapepod.info}
This manual.
@item @file{/etc/escapepod/config.toml}
The service's configuration (not shipped; @file{schemas/config.schema.json}).
@item NixOS @code{services.escapepod}
@code{enable}, @code{package}, @code{settings} (TOML), @code{statusUsers}.
@end table

Known consumers: the three package definitions in @file{packaging/}, the
NixOS module and its VM test.
